.TH MODMAN 8 "2026-05-05" "modman" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
modman \- pfs module manager (CLI backend for PuppyRus / rootaufs2 systems)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modman
[\fB--machine\fR]
[\fB-d\fR \fIDIR\fR | \fB--download-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB--progress-file\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB--lower\fR | \fB--upper\fR | \fB--toram\fR]
[\fB--load-cmd\fR \fICMD\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR
[\fIARGS\fR]
.PP
.B modman
[\fB--machine\fR]
\fB--remove-local\fR|\fB-Rl\fR
\fINAME\fR [\fINAME\fR ...]
.PP
.B modman -h
|
.B --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmodman\fR is the CLI backend that orchestrates discovery, download,
dependency resolution, install (\fIpfsload\fR) and remove (\fIpfsunload\fR)
of pfs container modules. It delegates filesystem-level operations to
\fBpfs-utils\fR (\fIpfs\fR(8), \fIpfsload\fR, \fIpfsunload\fR,
\fIpfsinfo\fR, \fIpfsbench\fR) and reads configuration from
\fImodman.conf\fR(5).
.PP
modman supports two CLI dialects switched by the \fBCLI_STYLE\fR config
key: \fIpacman\fR-style (\fB-S\fR, \fB-R\fR, \fB-Sy\fR, \fB-Ss\fR \(em the
default) and \fIapt\fR-style (\fBinstall\fR, \fBremove\fR, \fBupdate\fR,
\fBsearch\fR).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Maintenance / discovery
.TP
.B -mi \fIDIR\fR
Generate \fI000-index.txt\fR in \fIDIR\fR. Maintainer-only.
.TP
.B -di \fIDIR\fR
Generate \fI000-dependencies.txt\fR in \fIDIR\fR by extracting
\fIstart.sh\fR from each \fI*.${EXT}\fR present (default \fI.pfs\fR) and
parsing the \fB<pkg>-dep\fR lines. Maintainer-only.
.SS Cache sync
.TP
.B -Sy
.RB ( apt :
.BR update )
Pull \fI000-index.txt\fR and \fI000-dependencies.txt\fR from the first
non-commented entry of \fBREPO_URLS\fR. Stored in \fB${CACHE_DIR}\fR.
.SS Search
.TP
.B -Ss \fIQUERY\fR
.RB ( apt :
.BR "search QUERY" )
Substring search over the local index.
.SS Install / remove
.TP
.B -S \fIMODULE\fR
.RB ( apt :
.BR "install MODULE" )
Resolve dependencies for \fIMODULE\fR, download (\fIwget\fR), and
\fIpfsload\fR the result. \fIMODULE\fR may be:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
A name to look up in the local cache (\fB${CACHE_FILE}\fR), e.g.
.BR evince .
.IP \(bu 2
A path to an existing \fI*.${EXT}\fR file, e.g.
\fB/mnt/sr0/zz2601/modules/+/openssh-2601.pfs\fR
or
.BR ./openssh-2601.pfs .
A path is detected when the argument contains \fI/\fR, starts with
.I .
or
.IR ~ ,
points to a real file, and ends in
.IR .${EXT} .
Local-path mode skips cache lookup and download \(em dependencies are
still resolved from \fI${CACHE_DEP}\fR via \fIshort_pkgname\fR.
.RE
.TP
.B -R \fIMODULE\fR
.RB ( apt :
.BR "remove MODULE" )
Find a loaded module that matches \fIMODULE\fR (exact, short-name, or
prefix) and \fIpfsunload\fR it. Single match is resolved automatically;
multiple matches print a candidate list and exit non-zero.
.SS Listing
.TP
.B --list-local
Show files in \fB${DOWNLOAD_DIR}\fR.
.TP
.B --list-loaded
All currently loaded modules. Source: \fIpfsinfo --machine --mount\fR
with \fI/sys/fs/aufs\fR fallback. In \fB--machine\fR mode each line
has 6 TAB-separated fields:
.RS
.PP
\fIname\fR<TAB>\fIlayer\fR<TAB>\fIpath\fR<TAB>\fIversion\fR<TAB>\fImount_mode\fR<TAB>\fImount_in_ram\fR
.PP
\fImount_mode\fR is currently always empty (reserved for future use).
\fImount_in_ram\fR is \fByes\fR if the module's backing squashfs lives
on tmpfs, \fBno\fR otherwise, or empty when unknown.
.RE
.TP
.B --list-loaded-before
Modules loaded by initrd before system boot. Requires
\fBAUFS_INITRD_PREFIX\fR to be set or autodetectable
(\fIsee\fR \fIDEPENDENCY RESOLUTION\fR \fIand\fR \fIINITRD DETECTION\fR
below).
.TP
.B --list-loaded-after
Modules loaded after system boot.
.SS Remove local files
.TP
.B --remove-local \fINAME\fR [\fINAME\fR ...]
.RB ( "short:" " " -Rl )
Delete downloaded \fI*.${EXT}\fR files from \fB${DOWNLOAD_DIR}\fR.
Variadic: accepts one or more module names separated by spaces.
Both short name (\fBfoo\fR) and full filename (\fBfoo.pfs\fR) are
accepted \(em the \fI.${EXT}\fR suffix is stripped automatically.
.PP
Before deleting each file, mount status is checked via
\fIpfsinfo --machine --mount\fR. Mounted modules are rejected (file is
not deleted) but processing of remaining names continues.
.PP
Exit codes (aggregated, variadic mode):
.RS
.TP
.B 0
All files deleted successfully.
.TP
.B 7
At least one invalid module name.
.TP
.B 8
At least one module rejected (currently mounted).
.TP
.B 9
Other error (file not found, rm failure, permission denied).
.RE
.PP
Machine output format (--machine, TSV):
.RS
.TP
removed\et<name>\et<path>
File deleted successfully.
.TP
error\etmounted\et<name>
File is mounted \(em rejected.
.TP
error\etnot_found\et<name>\et<path>
File not found.
.TP
error\etinvalid_name\et<name>
Invalid module name.
.TP
error\etrm_failed\et<name>
rm(1) error.
.RE
.SS Update management
.PP
All update commands operate against the local cache (\fI${CACHE_DIR}/db.txt\fR).
The update check (\fB--check-updates\fR) never modifies files.
Applying updates (\fB--update\fR, \fB--update-all\fR) requires root.
.TP
.B --check-updates
Compare installed modules against the repository cache and print a list of
available updates. \fBDoes not apply updates automatically\fR and \fBdoes not
modify any file\fR. Safe to run without root. The login-time helper
(\fBmodman-update-check\fR) uses exactly this command and likewise
\fBdoes not apply updates automatically\fR.
.RS
.PP
In \fB--machine\fR mode each update line contains 11 TAB-separated fields:
.PP
.B update\etid\etname\etold_version\etnew_version\etinstalled_path\etcandidate_filename\etrepo\etrisk\etreboot_required\etmessage
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l l.
\fBField\fR@\fBValue\fR
update@Row type (literal)
id@Unique update identifier (for --update <id>)
name@Short module name (identity)
old_version@Currently installed version
new_version@Candidate version in repository
installed_path@Full path to the installed file
candidate_filename@Candidate filename in repository
repo@Source repository URL
risk@\fBnormal\fR | \fBloaded\fR | \fBsystem\fR
reboot_required@\fB0\fR or \fB1\fR
message@Human-readable message (empty or \fBblacklisted\fR)
.TE
.PP
The \fBrisk\fR field:
.RS
.TP
.B normal
Module is not loaded in the current session.
.TP
.B loaded
Module was loaded after system boot (hot-attached). Update is safe but
takes effect only after reboot or reconnection.
.TP
.B system
Module was loaded by initrd before system start. Requires
\fB--confirm-system-updates\fR.
.RE
.PP
The \fBreboot_required\fR field is \fB1\fR when the new module version
contains changes that require a reboot (e.g. kernel, initrd, base
libraries). In that case machine output includes an additional line:
.PP
.RS
.B \[u043D]\[u0443]\[u0436]\[u043D]\[u0430] \[u043F]\[u0435]\[u0440]\[u0435]\[u0437]\[u0430]\[u0433]\[u0440]\[u0443]\[u0437]\[u043A]\[u0430]
.RE
.PP
This literal Russian string (\(lqreboot required\(rq) is part of the
machine contract and appears verbatim in machine output, GUI display,
and \fIupdate.log\fR. Parsers must match it as a literal.
.RE
.TP
.B --update \fIID\fR
Apply a single update by identifier \fIID\fR from \fB--check-updates\fR
output. Downloads the candidate, replaces the installed file, saves a
backup with suffix \fI.old\fR (or \fI.old.N\fR for multiple backups).
Writes result to \fIupdate.log\fR.
.RS
.PP
System modules (\fBrisk=system\fR) are rejected with exit code \fB8\fR
unless \fB--confirm-system-updates\fR is passed.
.RE
.TP
.B --update-all
Apply all available updates from \fB--check-updates\fR. System modules
(\fBrisk=system\fR) are skipped without \fB--confirm-system-updates\fR
\(em they receive a \fBskipped\fR line in machine output but are not
counted as errors.
.RS
.PP
Exit codes:
.TP
.B 0
All updates applied successfully (skipped system modules are not errors).
.TP
.B 1
At least one update failed (download, rename, mv).
.RE
.TP
.B --confirm-system-updates
Global flag (like \fB--machine\fR): permits updating modules with
\fBrisk=system\fR. Without this flag \fB--update\fR exits with code
\fB8\fR and \fB--update-all\fR skips system modules.
.RS
.PP
.B WARNING:
updating system modules may require a reboot. Always check the
\fBreboot_required\fR field before applying.
.RE
.TP
.B --verbose-skips
Global flag: enables output of \fBskipped\fR lines in machine output for
modules skipped during \fB--update-all\fR (e.g. incomparable version or
no candidate). Without this flag skips are silent.
.RS
.PP
Format of a \fBskipped\fR line (4 fields):
.PP
.B skipped\etreason\etid\etmessage
.RE
.TP
.B --include-blacklisted
Global flag: includes blacklisted version entries in \fB--check-updates\fR
output. Such lines have \fBmessage=blacklisted\fR. Without this flag
blacklisted versions are silently skipped.
.TP
.B --update-blacklist-list
Print the contents of the update blacklist file. Each line:
\fBidentity\etversion\fR.
.TP
.B --update-blacklist-add \fIID-OR-CANDIDATE\fR
Add a version to the blacklist. Accepts a full candidate filename
(\fIfoo-1.1.pfs\fR) or just the identity (\fIfoo\fR) \(em in the latter
case the cache is searched to determine the latest version.
.TP
.B --update-blacklist-remove \fIIDENTITY\fR \fIVERSION\fR
Remove a specific entry from the blacklist by identity and version.
.SS Machine output: update lines
.PP
In \fB--machine\fR mode the update commands emit the following line types:
.TP
.B update\etid\etname\etold_version\etnew_version\etinstalled_path\etcandidate_filename\etrepo\etrisk\etreboot_required\etmessage
Available update (from \fB--check-updates\fR). 11 fields.
.TP
.B applied\etid\etold_path\etnew_path\etbackup_path\etrisk\etreboot_required\etmessage
Update applied successfully. 8 fields.
.TP
.B skipped\etreason\etid\etmessage
Update skipped (only with \fB--verbose-skips\fR or for system modules
without \fB--confirm-system-updates\fR). 4 fields.
.TP
.B error\etreason\etid\etmessage
Error applying update. 4 fields.
.SS Exit codes (update commands)
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Update application error (download, mv, rename).
.TP
.B 7
Invalid argument (module name, id).
.TP
.B 8
System module (\fBrisk=system\fR) without \fB--confirm-system-updates\fR.
.SS Help
.TP
.B -h, --help, help
Print built-in help. Triggered by no argument as well.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --machine
TSV output suitable for parsing. Suppresses colored / human
\fIprint_msg\fR output but preserves \fIprint_err\fR / \fIfatal_err\fR
on stderr.
.TP
.B -d \fIDIR\fR, --download-dir \fIDIR\fR
Override
.B DOWNLOAD_DIR
for the current invocation. Wins over both \fImodman.conf\fR and
autodetect (\fIpfs --download-dir\fR). Useful when the autodetected
directory is read-only (e.g. live ISO mount).
.TP
.B --progress-file \fIPATH\fR, --progress-file=\fIPATH\fR
Sink for machine-readable download progress. Equivalent to setting
the
.B MODMAN_PROGRESS_FILE
environment variable, but survives
.B pkexec
privilege escalation (which strips non-whitelisted env vars). Used by
\fImodman-gui\fR to drive its progress bar. The file is rewritten on
each tick with three lines: \fIname=<module>\fR, \fIstage=download\fR,
\fIpct=<0..100>\fR.
.TP
.B --lower
Pass \fI-l\fR to \fIpfsload\fR \(em install module to lower AUFS layer.
Mutually exclusive with \fB--upper\fR.
.TP
.B --upper
Pass \fI-u\fR to \fIpfsload\fR \(em install module to upper AUFS layer
(this is \fIpfsload\fR's built-in default).
.TP
.B --toram
Pass \fI-r\fR to \fIpfsload\fR \(em copy module to tmpfs before mounting.
Combinable with \fB--lower\fR or \fB--upper\fR.
.TP
.B --load-cmd \fICMD\fR
Override \fICMD_LOAD\fR with full command string \fICMD\fR. Word-split
on whitespace; final argv is \fICMD\fR + module path. Used by GUI
right-click menu when \fIPFSLOAD_ALLOW_*\fR conf keys provide custom
commands. NOT compatible with \fB--lower/--upper/--toram\fR.
.SH SHORT ALIASES
Short aliases are available for frequently used commands. Behaviour is
identical to the long form; both forms are accepted in both dialects
(pacman-style and apt-style).
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l l l.
\fBLong form\fR@\fBShort alias\fR@\fBMnemonic\fR
--list-loaded@-L@List loaded
--list-loaded-before@-Lb@List loaded \(em before
--list-loaded-after@-La@List loaded \(em after
--list-local@-Ql@Query local
--remove-local@-Rl@Remove local
.TE
.SH DEPENDENCY RESOLUTION
.SS Source of truth
Each \fI.pfs\fR module ships a \fIstart.sh\fR script. Maintainer encodes
dependencies as lines of the form:
.PP
.RS
.B <pkg>-dep <dep1> <dep2> <dep3>
.RE
.SS Maintainer side: \fImodman -di\fR
For every \fI*.${EXT}\fR in the target directory:
.IP "1." 4
Extract \fIstart.sh\fR via \fIunsquashfs -cat\fR.
.IP "2." 4
Grep regex \fB[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+-dep [ A-Za-z0-9_-]+\fR.
.IP "3." 4
Strip the \fB<pkg>-dep\fR prefix; keep the dep list.
.IP "4." 4
Append \fBshortname : dep1 dep2 ...\fR to \fI000-dependencies.txt\fR.
.PP
mtime cache: if the \fI.pfs\fR is older than the existing
\fI000-dependencies.txt\fR, the cached entry is reused instead of
re-running \fIunsquashfs\fR.
.SS Client side: \fImodman -Sy\fR
.PP
.RS
\fBwget -qO\fR \fI${CACHE_DEP}\fR.tmp \fI<repo_url>/000-dependencies.txt\fR
.br
\fBmv\fR \fI${CACHE_DEP}\fR.tmp \fI${CACHE_DEP}\fR
.RE
.PP
A 404 leaves \fI${CACHE_DEP}\fR truncated to empty.
.SS \fIshort_pkgname\fR normalisation
The cache key is the \fIshortname\fR \(em the file basename minus
\fI.${EXT}\fR with the following regex applied:
.PP
.RS
\fBs/(-[0-9].*|_any.*|_64.*|-sf[0-9]+.*|-au[0-9]+.*)//\fR
.RE
.PP
Strips: version (\fI-3.26.0...\fR), arch (\fI_64\fR / \fI_any\fR),
revision tags (\fI-sf06\fR / \fI-au01\fR).
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l l.
\fBfull name\fR@\fBshortname\fR
evince-gtk3-p-3.26.0_64-sf06.pfs@evince-gtk3-p
030-gtk3-2601-sf03.pfs@030-gtk3
chromium-bin-gtk3-p-1.0_64-sf01.pfs@chromium-bin-gtk3-p
.TE
.SS Resolution at \fImodman -S\fR
.PP
.RS
.nf
shortname=$(short_pkgname "$name")
deps=$(grep "^$shortname :" "$CACHE_DEP" | cut -d':' -f2- | sed 's/^ *//')

for dep in $deps; do
    _validate_name "$dep"           # safety: [a-zA-Z0-9._+-]
    _dep_is_ignored "$dep" && continue
    "$0" $MACHINE_FLAG -S "$dep"    # recursive subprocess
done
.fi
.RE
.PP
Recursion is implemented as fresh
.B "$0" -S
subprocess invocations, not internal function calls. Each dep separately
re-reads the cache, resolves its own deps, downloads and \fIpfsload\fRs.
.SH INITRD DETECTION
\fBmodman\fR delegates initrd-aware logic to \fBpfs-utils\fR which uses
a plugin directory of detector scripts:
.PP
.RS
\fI${INITRD_DETECTORS_DIR}\fR (default
\fI/usr/local/lib/pfs-utils/initrd-detectors/\fR)
.RE
.PP
Each \fINN-name.sh\fR sources a \fIdetect_<name>()\fR function that
returns 0 on match and sets globals \fBINITRD_NAME\fR,
\fBINITRD_LAYERING\fR, \fBINITRD_AUFS_PREFIX\fR,
\fBINITRD_DOWNLOAD_DIR\fR. The dispatcher iterates files in lex order
(numeric prefix = precedence) and the first match wins.
.PP
Shipped detectors:
.TS
tab(@);
l l l l.
\fBfile\fR@\fBinitrd\fR@\fBlayering\fR@\fBaufs prefix\fR
10-uird.sh@uird@overlay@${SYSMNT}/bundles
20-rootaufs2.sh@rootaufs2@aufs@/run/archroot/live/memory/images
30-porteus.sh@porteus@aufs@${SYSMNT}/bundles
40-livekit.sh@livekit@overlay@${SYSMNT}/bundles
.TE
.PP
Adding a new initrd type is a drop-in: place \fI50-yourname.sh\fR with
the contract described above; no edits to the \fIpfs\fR library are
needed.
.SH AUTODETECT FALLBACK
\fBmodman\fR uses the following resolution order for the
initrd-derived knobs:
.IP "1." 4
\fBconfig\fR \(em value set in \fImodman.conf\fR(5).
.IP "2." 4
\fBCLI override\fR \(em \fB-d\fR for \fBDOWNLOAD_DIR\fR.
.IP "3." 4
\fBautodetect\fR \(em shell out to \fIpfs --aufs-initrd-prefix\fR or
\fIpfs --download-dir\fR.
.PP
If autodetect fails (no detector matches or \fIdir=\fR absent in
\fI/proc/cmdline\fR), the value stays empty. Commands that actually
consume the missing var print a clear stderr error and \fBexit 1\fR;
unrelated commands (\fI--help\fR, \fI--list-local\fR with explicit
\fBDOWNLOAD_DIR\fR, \fI--list-loaded\fR without filter) keep working.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The following keys are read from \fImodman.conf\fR(5). They control the
right-click context menu in \fBmodman-gui\fR and the \fB--load-cmd\fR
CLI option.
.TP
.B PFSLOAD_ALLOW_LOWER
Right-click menu command for "Load to lower layer". String value
holds full command (e.g. \fIpfsload -l\fR). Empty/absent \(-> menu item hidden.
.TP
.B PFSLOAD_ALLOW_TORAM
Right-click menu command for "Load to RAM" (e.g. \fIpfsload -r\fR).
.TP
.B PFSLOAD_ALLOW_LOWER_TORAM
Right-click menu command for "lower layer + RAM" (e.g. \fIpfsload -l -r\fR).
.TP
.B PFSLOAD_ALLOW_UPPER_TORAM
Right-click menu command for "upper layer + RAM" (e.g. \fIpfsload -u -r\fR).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Plain install
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo modman -S evince
.fi
.RE
.SS Skip pre-bundled deps
\fImodman.conf\fR:
.PP
.RS
\fBMODMAN_IGNORE_DEPS="030-gtk3"\fR
.RE
.PP
modman skips \fB030-gtk3\fR with an info message instead of recursing
into install.
.SS Override download dir (autodetect path is read-only)
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo modman -d /tmp/modman-cache -S evince
.fi
.RE
.SS Install local file
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo modman -S /mnt/sr0/zz2601/modules/+/openssh-2601.pfs
sudo modman -S ./openssh-2601.pfs
.fi
.RE
.SS Remove by short name
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo modman -R evince
.fi
.RE
\fBmodman\fR resolves \fBevince\fR to the loaded
\fBevince-gtk3-p-3.26.0_64-sf06\fR via \fIpfsinfo --machine --mount\fR.
.SS Machine-readable listing for downstream parsers
.PP
.RS
.nf
modman --machine --list-loaded-before
.fi
.RE
.SS Remove local file
.PP
.RS
.nf
modman --remove-local evince
modman -Rl evince evince-gtk3-p
.fi
.RE
.SS Check for updates (safe, no root needed)
.PP
.RS
.nf
modman --machine --check-updates
.fi
.RE
.SS Apply a single update
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo modman --update <id>
.fi
.RE
.SS Apply all updates, including system modules
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo modman --update-all --confirm-system-updates
.fi
.RE
.SH CAVEATS
.SS Dependency cycles
A circular dep graph (A \(-> B \(-> A) causes infinite recursion. There
is no
.B visited
set; the operator must avoid such graphs at \fI-di\fR generation time.
.SS Diamond dependencies
A \(-> B, A \(-> C, B \(-> C results in C being installed twice. There is
no memoisation across the recursive subprocess tree.
.SS No version constraints
\fI<pkg>-dep\fR lines list dep
.B names
only. There is no SemVer-style \fB>=1.0\fR; whichever version is in the
cache wins.
.SS No topological sort
Dependencies are processed in the order extracted by the regex; pre-order
tree expansion. Parallel install is not supported.
.SS Already-loaded deps
A dep that is already \fIpfsload\fR-ed is still re-installed
unconditionally. \fIpfsload\fR may report an error or a no-op depending
on the layering mode.
.SS Dep missing from cache
If \fImodman -S dep\fR fails because the dep is not present in
\fI${CACHE_FILE}\fR, the parent install continues with the next dep
(loop iteration).
.B MODMAN_IGNORE_DEPS
is the recommended way to silence such cases when the dep is bundled
into a base module.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/modman.conf
System-wide configuration. See \fImodman.conf\fR(5).
.TP
.I ~/.config/modman/modman.conf
Per-user override.
.TP
.I ${CACHE_DIR}/db.txt
Local cache of \fI000-index.txt\fR (default \fI/var/cache/modman/db.txt\fR).
.TP
.I ${CACHE_DIR}/dependencies.txt
Local cache of \fI000-dependencies.txt\fR.
.TP
.I ${DOWNLOAD_DIR}
Where downloaded \fI*.${EXT}\fR files land. Default for rootaufs2 is
autodetected as \fI/mnt/home/${dir}/optional\fR.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/pfs-utils/initrd-detectors/
Plugin directory for initrd detector scripts (provided by
\fBpfs-utils-cli\fR).
